  "transform_code": "def transform(df: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"\n    Transform raw dataset into analysis-ready dataframe.\n\n    Steps:\n    - Ensure outcome is binary and numeric.\n    - Create clear/explicit columns for focal and other group sizes and distances.\n    - Compute relative size (focal - other) and a ratio.\n    - Define a binary location advantage indicator (LocFocal): 1 if contest location is closer to focal group's home-center than to other group's home-center, else 0.\n    - Provide a small set of controls (male counts) and drop rows with missing values in key variables.\n\n    Note: The original schema contains some ambiguous column descriptions (e.g., 'win' and 'm_focal' used for distances). Here we follow the convention used in the analysis: 'win' -> distance from focal group center; 'm_focal' -> distance from other group center.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Make a copy to avoid modifying in place\n    df = df.copy()\n\n    # Ensure binary outcome\n    if 'dyad' not in df.columns:\n        raise ValueError(\"Expected column 'dyad' in input dataframe\")\n    df['ContestOutcome'] = pd.to_numeric(df['dyad'], errors='coerce').astype('float')\n\n    # Create/rename distance columns (use documented mapping from schema)\n    # 'win' appears in the dataset as distance of focal group from its home-center\n    # 'm_focal' appears as distance of the other group from its home-center\n    df['DistFocalCenter'] = pd.to_numeric(df['win'], errors='coerce')\n    df['DistOtherCenter'] = pd.to_numeric(df['m_focal'], errors='coerce')\n\n    # Create clear size columns. The original schema is ambiguous about f_focal/f_other naming,\n    # but columns exist with these names. We preserve both and define FocalSize and OtherSize from them.\n    # Based on typical naming in many datasets we treat 'f_focal' as the focal group's total size and\n    # 'f_other' as the other group's total size. If this mapping is reversed in your version, swap them.\n    df['FocalSize'] = pd.to_numeric(df['f_focal'], errors='coerce')\n    df['OtherSize'] = pd.to_numeric(df['f_other'], errors='coerce')\n\n    # Relative size: focal minus other\n    df['RelGroupSize'] = df['FocalSize'] - df['OtherSize']\n\n    # Relative size ratio (for diagnostics / alternative models)\n    df['RelSizeRatio'] = df['FocalSize'] / df['OtherSize'].replace({0: np.nan})\n\n    # Create binary location indicator: 1 if contest location is closer to focal center than other center\n    # Use strict less-than; ties go to '0' (not focal advantage). If you want a neutral category, modify accordingly.\n    df['LocFocal'] = (df['DistFocalCenter'] < df['DistOtherCenter']).astype('int')\n\n    # Preserve male counts (controls). Ensure numeric.\n    df['n_focal'] = pd.to_numeric(df['n_focal'], errors='coerce')\n    df['other'] = pd.to_numeric(df['other'], errors='coerce')\n\n    # Optional derived controls\n    df['MaleDiff'] = df['n_focal'] - df['other']\n\n    # Drop rows with missing values in variables required for the main model\n    required_cols = ['ContestOutcome', 'RelGroupSize', 'LocFocal', 'n_focal', 'other', 'FocalSize', 'OtherSize', 'DistFocalCenter', 'DistOtherCenter']\n    df = df.dropna(subset=required_cols)\n\n    # Ensure ContestOutcome is integer 0/1\n    df['ContestOutcome'] = df['ContestOutcome'].astype(int)\n\n    return df\n",
